# Frontend domain & side actions

## Identity

- Prefer `user_id` for aggregation, signup maps, and score sync displays that drive logic.
- Display names are render-time only (`user_display_names` / user fields) - do not reintroduce name-keyed maps.

## Director capabilities

- Gate management UI with director-access / `useTournamentManagementAccess` patterns - not "any TD sees everything."

## Side-action UI

- Prefer thin hooks (`useBracketActions`) + focused components/tables/modals over a monolithic tab.
- Config forms imported by parents or unit mounts **must remain resolvable**; deleting a form without grepping importers breaks CI.
- Disabled / "coming soon" types are fine as UI copy, but tests must assert the **current** shipped panel (`Side Action`, `Director setup`, create CTA, etc.).
- Prefer existing diagram adapter surfaces for match-play scoring UIs already migrated away from React Flow, unless explicitly asked to reintroduce Flow.

## High Game / High Series / Eliminator lessons

- Live standings come from GET standings endpoints — do **not** wire `calculate-winners`, `process-cuts`, or result POSTs (retired / 410 on the backend).
- Share handicap + open-pot financials UI (`HandicapConfigSection`, `OpenPotFinancialsSection`); keep type-specific window/drop/game checkbox logic in the type form.
- Extract list tables per type (`BracketSideActionsTable`, `HighGameSideActionsTable`, `HighSetSideActionsTable`, `EliminatorSideActionsTable`) instead of growing `SideActionsTab`.
- Report menu defs live in `reports/reportMenuDefs.ts`; report HTTP types/methods in `src/api/side-action-reports.ts` (re-exported from `side-actions.ts` is fine).
- Keep `SideActionReportsMenuModal` thin: option panels / builders go in `reports/*ReportOptionPanels.tsx` and `reports/openPotReportBuilders.ts` (CI size gate).
- Client mirrors of backend math (`eliminatorProjection`, fund helpers, game-plan validation) need unit tests that match the backend examples.
- `game_numbers` is the only game-plan source of truth and may be non-contiguous. Never synthesize contiguous windows from `starting_game` / `num_games`.
- After a backend SSOT change: grep `src/api` for unused legacy methods and delete them in the same delivery.
